\frametitle{Example (sketch)}
\small
\begin{columns}[T]
\begin{column}{0.48\textwidth}
\textbf{Page / excerpt}\\[0.3em]
\texttt{\ldots Scope 1 emissions 2019:}\\
\texttt{772,607 kgCO2e \ldots}
\end{column}
\begin{column}{0.48\textwidth}
\textbf{Trace (snippet)}\\[0.3em]
\textit{``Need to extract Scope~1 \ldots}\\
\textit{table shows 772607 \ldots}\\
\textit{unit is kgCO2e \ldots''}
\end{column}
\end{columns}
\vspace{0.8em}
\textbf{Final answer (JSON)}\\[0.3em]
{\ttfamily \{"KPI\_Entries": [\{"year": 2019, "kpi\_name": "1",}\\
{\ttfamily "value": 772607, "unit": "kgCO2e"\}]\}}
\vspace{0.6em}
\begin{alertblock}{For discussion}
What counts as ``good'' reasoning -- length, correct number,
link to the page, revision, \ldots?
